  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In desktop mode, when using the SPOUT camera with the camera window closed, if someone is flying a camera within the view of your camera (the SPOUT view) and you press esc to open the quick menu, the red vertical and directional camera indicator lines appear on the SPOUT camera image as well as locally. These red vertical and directional indicator lines should not output to the SPOUT camera view.\n\n1. Start a streaming camera and enable a SPOUT stream\n\n2. Close the camera window (leaving the SPOUT camera active)\n\n3. Press the esc key in desktop mode when someone is flying a camera in front of the SPOUT view\n\n4. The red vertical and direction lines appear for the camera, but no camera puck is visible\n\nOnly tested on PC in desktop mode, the same issue might also apply to VR mode though.",
